Hi {{first_name}} -

Centers like {{center}} are measured on how many job seekers land and what they earn. White-collar workers are often the hardest to move: 28% of unemployed white-collar workers are still looking after 27 weeks, up from 23% a year ago (our monthly report: https://launchyournextchapter.com/reports/white-collar-employment-report-september-2026?utm_source=cold&utm_medium=email&utm_content=ajc). {{line_local}}

I founded NextChapter, the leading job transition platform. Each person gets a pivot plan from their work history, retraining for the gaps (open AI-titled roles in our database advertise about a third more than others at the same level), networking outreach drafted, coaching, and exclusive jobs and recruiters. {{line_open_roles}}

It is free to the people you refer, and we report how many engaged, interviewed and landed, as counts only, so you can see the outcome you are measured on.

I can send a one-page handout with a QR code for your front desk. May I send it?
